# Judge adapters

This repo does not wrap an xAI SDK. Judges are fresh, toolless CLI processes (`claude`, `codex`, `grok`). There is no `llm/` client module and no live call in the default tests.

- One fresh process per (judge, task). Session reuse would fake the correlation this repo measures.
- Timeouts, missing binaries, and unparseable output are `error` verdicts, not endorsements. `QuotaExhausted` halts the panel; it does not guess.
- Served-model provenance uses requested-when-proven-else-dominant. Do not take the first `modelUsage` entry (ancillary models are listed first).
- `PROMPT_VERSION` is provenance only. Never fold it into `cache_key`.
- Binary resolution is env override (`QC_CODEX_BIN`, `QC_GROK_BIN`), then PATH, then a hard error. No personal fallback paths.
- Tests use recorded fixtures or a fake judge function. No live CLI calls in CI.
